Question("sign-meaning-D12", "sign-D12", Category.RULES, "Which description identifies this illustrated Swedish sign, symbol or road marking?", listOf(Option("Required direction for specified dangerous-goods vehicles", "D12 · Required direction for specified dangerous-goods vehicles. Vehicles carrying loads subject to the dangerous-goods orange-plate marking requirement must follow the indicated direction. If a letter is shown, the instruction applies only to vehicles barred from a tunnel of that category.", ""), Option("Cottage accommodation", "H10 · Cottage accommodation. Identifies an establishment with a small number of cottages. Check its actual accommodation arrangements and availability.", ""), Option("Stop line", "M13 · Stop line. This identifies where to stop when a sign or signal requires it. The line alone does not create a universal stop duty.", ""), Option("Additional lane", "F16 · Additional lane. The number of lanes increases. Read the diagram for direction and any physical separation.", "")), 0, "Vehicles carrying loads subject to the dangerous-goods orange-plate marking requirement must follow the indicated direction. If a letter is shown, the instruction applies only to vehicles barred from a tunnel of that category.", 333, "https://www.transportstyrelsen.se/sv/vagtrafik/trafikregler-och-vagmarken/vagmarken/pabudsmarken/pabjuden-korriktning-for-fordon-lastat-med-farligt-gods/", "curriculum/h1-d12.png", rewrite9E5Node000659()),
