Question("sign-meaning-M10", "sign-M10", Category.RULES, "Which description identifies this illustrated Swedish sign, symbol or road marking?", listOf(Option("Broken line beside a continuous line", "M10 · Broken line beside a continuous line. The continuous line governs a driver on its side of the marking. Do not treat the broken line on the other side as permission to change lanes.", ""), Option("Radio station for traffic information", "G3 · Radio station for traffic information. Identifies a radio station with regular recurring road-traffic information broadcasts intended to cover a wider area. Read the station or frequency shown.", ""), Option("Place reserved for a stated purpose", "C40 · Place reserved for a stated purpose. Read the stated purpose. A loading place concerns loading or unloading heavy or bulky goods, not unrestricted waiting.", ""), Option("No heavy lorries", "C7 · No heavy lorries. Traffic with heavy lorries is prohibited. Identify the vehicle class rather than assuming that every vehicle carrying goods is a heavy lorry.", "")), 0, "The continuous line governs a driver on its side of the marking. Do not treat the broken line on the other side as permission to change lanes.", 350, "https://www.transportstyrelsen.se/sv/vagtrafik/trafikregler-och-vagmarken/vagmarken/vagmarkeringar/mittlinje-eller-korfaltslinje-och-heldragen-linje/", "curriculum/ASSET-e02bf8a7f06b031f.png", rewrite9E10Node000981()),
